ation.\n\nStep 4: Temporary password issued\nNavigation: CoreID Admin Console → user profile → Reset Password\nSelect Generate Temporary Password. Leave Force change at next sign-in checked — this is the default and it must not be disabled.\n\n### Visual Inspection Report (Image 4 (inline, following the text above)) [Confidence: 0.90 / High]:\nThe image shows a screenshot of a password reset page for a user named \"J. Employee\" with a temporary password provided.\n\n* The page has a white background with black text and a blue button.\n\t+ The title of the page is \"Reset Password - J. Employee\".\n\t+ Below the title, there is a section labeled \"Temporary password\" with the password \"Tq7#mVr2IkLp9x\" displayed.\n\t+ A checkbox is available to force a change at the next sign-in.\n\t+ A blue button labeled \"Generate Temporary Password\" is present.\n* The left side of the page features a dark blue sidebar with white text.\n\t+ The sidebar includes links to various sections, such as \"Admin Console\", \"Dashboard\", \"Tickets\", \"Users\", \"Reports\", and \"Settings\".\n* The top of the page displays a gray bar with the text \"Signed in as: A. Rao (L1 Support - Password Reset Admin)\".\n\nThe page appears to be a standard password reset page, providing a temporary password for the user to access their account. The presence of a checkbox to force a change at the next sign-in suggests that the user may have previously set a password that needs to be updated. Overall, the page is well-organized and easy to navigate, making it simple for the user to reset their password.\n\nStep 5: Temporary password relayed securely\nNavigation: Phone / voice channel — not logged in CoreID\nRead the temporary password to the caller verbally over the verified phone line. Never send it by email, chat, or ticket comment in plain text. See [CISA's guidance on requiring strong passwords](https://www.cisa.gov/secure-our-world/require-strong-passwords) for the reasoning behind credential-h